Here's a game I've made. It's an FPS with destructible physics in the Blender Game Engine. It's really just a high score game. There's lots of other stuff I'd like to do with it, but this is how far I've got at the moment. And I'm thinking of entering it into the Blender Summer Game 2010 Competition as is.<br><br>You can download the game from the link in the info box below the YouTube video. Rate, subscribe and comment ; )<br><br><a href="http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hs9A0bkXjuI" class="postlink">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hs9A0bkXjuI</a><br><br>You can also just download the blend file which is attached to this post. It was all made in Blender 2.49b, with a nice (free) font for the score made by <a href="http://pheist.net/" class="postlink">http://pheist.net/</a>.<br><br>Thanks for taking a look. I hope you like it!<br>Toby<dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/download/file.php?id=587" class="postimage" alt="shot3.png" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl><br /><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/download/file.php?id=586" class="postimage" alt="shot2.png" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl><br /><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/download/file.php?id=585" class="postimage" alt="shot1.png" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7307">tleave2000</a> — Wed Nov 03, 2010 11:16 pm</p><hr />
